    "answer": {
      "short": "If $x=-3$, then $|-x|=3$, whereas $x=-3$. Absolute value must be non-negative; the correct identity is $|-x|=|x|$.",
      "worked": "Consider $x=-3$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}|-(-3)|&=|3|\\\\&=3\\end{aligned}$$\nRachel's statement would give $|-(-3)|=-3$, which is false because an absolute value is non-negative. The correct identity is $|-x|=|x|$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
